# Mod 2: breath to Amp at 100: the level follows the breath (dynamics), not just the gate
wait 200
tap SEL
tap SEL
expect view 9
spin K1 1
spin K2 2
expect par15 1
expect par16 2
spin K3 100
expect par17 100
shot mod2_amp.png
midi 90 39 64
midi B0 02 00
wait 100
expect amp 0
expect level 0
breath 0 127 50
wait 30
expect amp 100
expect level >5
breath 127 64 50
wait 30
expect amp 50
midi 80 39 00
wait 200
# nothing on the screen is stale
wait 50
expect stale 0
# Mod 2: velocity to Amp. A panel key has a fixed velocity (100), not the last MIDI note's
expect view 9
spin K1 4
expect par15 5
midi 90 39 10
wait 30
expect amp 13
midi 80 39 00
wait 200
key 4 down
wait 30
expect amp 79
key 4 up
wait 300
# Mod 1 and Mod 2: bite to Amp at 100. Full bite up is full level; full bite down mutes: each slot's
# gain stops at 0, so two below it don't multiply back up to full
spin K1 -3
expect par15 2
tap SEL
tap SEL
tap SEL
expect view 8
spin K1 2
spin K2 2
spin K3 100
expect par12 2
expect par13 2
expect par14 100
midi 90 39 64
breath 0 127 30
midi E0 7F 7F
wait 30
expect amp 100
midi E0 00 00
wait 30
expect amp 0
midi E0 00 40
midi 80 39 00
spin K1 -2
spin K3 -100
wait 200
